# Methodology disposition: preliminary LUTRAM context A

Actual Vivado2022.2 routed5ns result: setup+0.079ns,hold-0.135ns
(1248failing endpoints),pulse+1.8ns. This run is a local timing failure under
unchanged input/output min0.1/max0.8ns budgets and uncertainty0.1ns.

Exact timing-object audit classified all1248negative hold paths as input-interface
paths; none is internal. The separately constrained register-to-register worst
hold is+0.010ns. No clock, internal-endpoint, input/output-delay, combinational-loop
or latch-loop checks are missing (all12check_timing categories0).

Methodology has32SYNTH-5 warnings, all existing enumerator replacement arrays
mapped to distributedRAM for timing. No TIMING rule violation is reported. These
are reported mappings, not waivers. DRC has oneRTSTAT-10 aggregate; exact net/pin
queries classify all1573affectednets as externaloutput-only, with no internal
consumer omitted. OOC output stubs/board timing remain unqualified.

This A context's FIFO2 payloads were also inferred as distributedRAM. That did
not alter logical FIFO behavior but failed the intended explicitFF launch
implementation. B sets RAM_STYLE=registers; allfour simulation suites prove
identical pin traces and cycles. A is retained as an intermediate result, not
relabelled as the finalFF implementation. No XDC was relaxed and no path waiver,
false path or multicycle exception was introduced. The external-budget failure
is not solved by adding arbitrary registers or changing min delay.

Ross timing-methodology skill requires2026.1+ for its JSON path; actual installed
2022.2 uses text report_methodology/check_timing and direct timing/net objects.
SYNTH-5 is outside the skill's TIMING1–57 reference set; its actual instance list
and mapping are retained in methodology.rpt.
